+# PromptHMR Gate A/B audit
+
+Date: 2026-08-22 (Asia/Shanghai)
+Repository commit: `3b566b7dbb28ce506c7ea972c18693f4c705ce8c`
+Scope reached: Gate A complete; Gate B environment, local caches, and all lawful non-SPEC prediction assets complete; offline PHMR strict-load passed; Development not started.
+
+## 1. Gate A: scientific comparability
+
+### Decision
+
+PromptHMR is a valuable multi-person baseline for EgoBody, EgoHumans, and Harmony4D. It is not a single-person method:
+
+- the default video path detects several people, propagates a SAM2 mask per person, and retains native temporal `track_id` values;
+- the image model predicts all prompted people in a frame jointly (`TRANSFORMER: cross-person`);
+- the video head runs per native track and produces temporally coherent SMPL-X parameters;
+- masked DROID-Calib estimates one camera trajectory, and `world.py` applies that same trajectory to every person, producing one world frame per input sequence;
+- `camera_world` exports `Rwc/Twc` and the inverse `Rcw/Tcw`, while every person exports `smplx_world`.
+
+The relevant entry point is the world-video pipeline used by `scripts/demo_video.py` / `pipeline.Pipeline`. It accepts either a video or an ordered JPEG directory. `scripts/demo_phmr.py` is single-view and is not a valid baseline for the three current multi-person video datasets. `scripts/eval_phmr.py` only covers the repository's stock benchmark annotations and is not the execution entry point for our frozen manifests.
+
+### Important limitation relative to Bridge3R
+
+PromptHMR supports a moving or static **single monocular camera sequence**, but has no explicit shot-boundary reset, cross-shot transaction, multi-camera gauge alignment, or camera-stitching module. Its default path assumes:
+
+- one continuous SLAM problem;
+- one focal length / principal point for the whole input;
+- one tracker propagation over the whole input.
+
+Therefore a frozen CS150 input formed by concatenating two views at frame 75 is a legitimate end-to-end robustness comparison, but it is not a native multi-camera mode of PromptHMR. The paper must disclose that PromptHMR is run unchanged over the concatenated RGB sequence and that it has no boundary-aware state reset. This mismatch is part of the problem being evaluated, not a reason to hide crashes, missed people, ID breaks, or low coverage.
+
+### Fair protocol implication
+
+For a direct table, run the default moving-camera world-video path on exactly the same prediction-only RGB manifests and keep all failures in coverage. Do not use the single-image demo, inject GT boxes/IDs/calibration, manually repair cross-view identities, or set `--static-camera` merely because it improves a Development case. Any no-SPEC execution must be named an adapted variant rather than the unmodified official default.
+
+## 2. License gates
+
+PromptHMR itself is licensed only for non-commercial scientific research/education/artistic use and prohibits redistribution. Raw checkpoints, body models, repository code, and raw `results.pkl` files must not be included in a public artifact.
+
+The embedded `pipeline/spec/cam_calib.py` states that use requires a valid MPG license agreement or a right granted by an authorized party. The stock `Pipeline.__call__` executes `run_cam_calib(..., method='spec')` unconditionally before tracking; merely setting `use_spec_calib: false` does **not** prevent SPEC execution. Consequently:
+
+- `data/pretrain/camcalib_sa_biased_l2.ckpt` was deliberately not downloaded;
+- no SPEC module/model import or inference was executed in this audit;
+- the official-default Development run remains blocked until the user confirms a valid right;
+- without that right, a code adapter must skip the `run_cam_calib` block and disable the later SPEC gravity transform, and results must be labeled `PromptHMR (no-SPEC adapter)`.
+
+The existing SMPL/SMPL-X symlinks target the user's local licensed Movie3R assets. No body model was copied or downloaded from a community mirror. The constructor helper `data/body_models/smplx2smpl_joints.npy` was derived locally from those authorized SMPL assets plus the public nine-extra-joint regressor already present in both the ROMP and TRAM checkouts. The final 33-row helper is shape-compatible with, and agrees within `2.9802322e-08` of, the same buffer stored in the PromptHMR image checkpoint. It is a local derived asset and must not be redistributed. `data/body_models/smplx/SMPLX_neutral_array_f32_slim.npz` remains absent and only blocks the final MCS export; `results.pkl` is written before that export.
+
